  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Ozone is a very reactive allotrope of oxygen. The reaction of ozone with alkenes and alkynes causes the oxidative cleaving of the alkene or alkyne. The carbon-carbon double bonds are replaced with carbon-oxygen double bonds, giving the required carbonyl product as shown below.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/e77ae704-4bcf-420c-a398-3f57ef5a9af5-6a3d76ae-7a7f-46e0-a6de-46c9c658d93c-image.png\" style=\"width: 420px; height: 217px;\" /></p><p>In all other options both compounds will give the same product on ozonolysis.</p></blockquote>",
